NAME
.in +5
.br
.bd
echo
- echo arguments
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SYNTAX
.in +5
.br
.bd
echo [ -n ] [ arg ... ]
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
DESCRIPTION
.in +5
.br
Echo writes its arguments to the standard output, separated by single
spaces and followed by a newline.
.sp
-n suppresses the newline.  It is recognised only as the first
argument, and only written exactly so; "echo -n -n" writes the second
one out.
.sp
Echo is used by shell scripts that need to produce diagnostics or
prompt without a trailing newline.
.sp 2
.in -5
